  "reason": "Evidence: The top-performing configurations all use scvi_n200 (RNA) + multiprofile, with transformer+weighted (config_001, 0.725) and transformer+concat (config_032, 0.721) as the best. Weighted fusion consistently outperforms concat with transformer aggregation, and scvi_n200 is the clear best RNA encoder. The only untested multimodal+multiprofile+scvi_n200 configs are config_016 (resnet50, avgpool, weighted) and config_049 (resnet50, avgpool, concat). Question: Whether the weighted-fusion advantage holds under avgpool aggregation with resnet50, providing a data point on the aggregation×fusion interaction for the resnet50 backbone. Why this is the best last experiment: It is the closest untested variant to the proven best-performing family (scvi_n200 + multiprofile + weighted fusion), giving the highest expected accuracy among remaining options (~0.70-0.71). It is unlikely to beat config_001's 0.725, but it is the most rational exploitation of existing evidence. Expected cost: moderate, roughly 4-5 GPU hours (avgpool is cheaper than transformer; resnet50 is comparable to vit_l), keeping total budget around 41-42 GPU hours."
